<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Lobkowicz</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lobkowicz family</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Lobkowicz is a Bohemian noble family recorded from the fourteenth century, raised to princely rank in 1624. Its members included the chancellor Zdeněk Vojtěch Popel of Lobkowicz and Prince Václav Eusebius, who acquired the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagan">Sagan</a> in 1646. Prince Joseph Franz Maximilian was a patron of Beethoven. Its collections, confiscated under communism, were largely restored after 1989.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-lobkowicz.jpg" alt="House of Lobkowicz" width="320" height="383" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lobkowitz-fuerstliches-Wappen.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
